-What would be your word, Noel?

708
00:31:43,568 --> 00:31:44,694
-Good question.
-Mine would be…

709
00:31:45,445 --> 00:31:47,948
-[in English] "Love."
-[all exclaiming]

710
00:31:49,533 --> 00:31:50,617
Love, love, love.

711
00:31:50,700 --> 00:31:52,744
[in Japanese] As much as I'd like
to jump right into catching up,

712
00:31:52,828 --> 00:31:55,163
I've gotta prep something really quick.
Wait here.

713
00:31:55,247 --> 00:31:57,249
-All right. Okay, okay.
-Just for a minute.

714
00:31:57,332 --> 00:31:59,251
-You'll be back shortly, yeah?
-Then… We've gotta…

715
00:31:59,334 --> 00:32:02,254
-We'll go get ready too. We'll be quick.
-What? What're you getting ready for?

716
00:32:02,337 --> 00:32:04,256
Now we look like the selfish ones
who didn't bring anything.

717
00:32:04,339 --> 00:32:05,841
What're they gearing up to do?
We didn't prepare anything.

718
00:32:05,924 --> 00:32:07,050
We have our souvenirs. It's okay.

719
00:32:10,554 --> 00:32:11,471
[laughing]

720
00:32:11,555 --> 00:32:12,556
-[Genta] Did he really?
-[Umi] He said…

721
00:32:12,639 --> 00:32:13,807
-[Shizu] I did not.
-You got red in the face.

722
00:32:13,890 --> 00:32:15,642
-Knock it off.
-[Shizu] I said no such thing.

723
00:32:15,725 --> 00:32:16,977
[band members exclaiming]

724
00:32:17,060 --> 00:32:19,813
-This is super! It's the best! Clap you!
-Thank you for waiting.

725
00:32:19,896 --> 00:32:22,566
This is fantastic! Clap, clap!
It's the best!

726
00:32:22,649 --> 00:32:24,818
-[Umi] Tacos!
-[Genta] Yumilicious!

727
00:32:24,901 --> 00:32:27,904
-I practiced hard to make these for you.
-What?

728
00:32:27,988 --> 00:32:28,989
-You made these?
-Are you serious?

729
00:32:29,072 --> 00:32:30,365
-[Noel] Dead serious.
-No way!

730
00:32:30,448 --> 00:32:33,618
-You really made these?
-I've worked here for the past week.

731
00:32:33,702 --> 00:32:34,703
-Oh, what?
-Like, actually?

732
00:32:34,786 --> 00:32:37,414
-[Shime] Wait, seriously? Really?
-What are you up to? That's too funny.

733
00:32:37,497 --> 00:32:42,502
I practiced hard because I wanted you
to enjoy the food I made. Please enjoy.

734
00:32:42,586 --> 00:32:45,630
-You crack me up, man!
-I'm ready to dig in.

735
00:32:45,714 --> 00:32:50,218
Hold on, you're saying you took orders
from the people here, and…

736
00:32:50,302 --> 00:32:51,595
-I did.
-That's awesome.

737
00:32:51,678 --> 00:32:53,722
-Right.
-Is that… why you've got that shirt on?

738
00:32:53,805 --> 00:32:56,266
I worked here.
I trained at this taco truck.

739
00:32:56,349 --> 00:32:57,392
Then these are Noel Tacos.

740
00:32:57,475 --> 00:32:58,643
Welcome to Noel Tacos.

741
00:32:58,727 --> 00:33:00,896
You mean, for the last few days,
you were a tacos chef,

742
00:33:00,979 --> 00:33:04,816
-not a Travis Japan member?
-Yes, I was a tacos chef. Tacos chef…

743
00:33:04,900 --> 00:33:06,318
[Genta] It's working up my appetite.

744
00:33:06,401 --> 00:33:10,906
Speaking of Travis Japan, let's kick off
with a cheer. We'll toast to this.

745
00:33:10,989 --> 00:33:12,991
-[Umi] By the way, what is it?
-[Genta] What is it?

746
00:33:13,825 --> 00:33:16,953
-Tequila.
-Tequila!

747
00:33:17,037 --> 00:33:19,623
-Amigo! Amigo!
-Amigo!

748
00:33:19,706 --> 00:33:23,043
-I'll fill your glasses.
-Oh, wait. It's in a special bottle.

749
00:33:23,126 --> 00:33:26,129
-Wow!
-[laughing]

750
00:33:26,922 --> 00:33:28,423
Awesome!

751
00:33:29,633 --> 00:33:31,259
-[Genta] This is awesome!
-Look at its color.

752
00:33:31,343 --> 00:33:32,969
-The color is amazing.
-The container is cute too.

753
00:33:33,053 --> 00:33:35,096
Whatever that container's supposed to be,
it sure is cute.

754
00:33:35,180 --> 00:33:38,683
-[laughs]
-Whoa!

755
00:33:38,767 --> 00:33:40,602
Oh, yeah. Thank you.

756
00:33:41,811 --> 00:33:45,273
-[Machu] Thanks.
-[exclaiming]

757
00:33:45,357 --> 00:33:46,441
-Hold on, Noel.
-[Shime] Sorry.

758
00:33:46,524 --> 00:33:47,692
Here.

759
00:33:48,193 --> 00:33:49,194
[Shime] Thank you!

760
00:33:49,277 --> 00:33:50,654
-I've got it.
-Oh, really?

761
00:33:52,948 --> 00:33:56,159
[all exclaiming]

762
00:33:56,243 --> 00:33:59,412
Okay, Chaka-chan.
Care to lead us, like usual?

763
00:34:00,121 --> 00:34:03,416
To our reunion…

764
00:34:03,500 --> 00:34:04,542
[laughs]

765
00:34:04,626 --> 00:34:05,835
To our reunion.

766
00:34:06,503 --> 00:34:09,839
-[in English] Cheers!
-[all] Cheers!

767
00:34:09,923 --> 00:34:11,800
Travis Japan!

768
00:34:11,883 --> 00:34:13,843
[cheering]

769
00:34:13,927 --> 00:34:16,930
[all] Amigo!

770
00:34:21,017 --> 00:34:22,394
-Yum.
-Wicked!

771
00:34:22,477 --> 00:34:25,146
-[Umi] Now that's refreshing!
-[Genta] Oh, yum.

772
00:34:25,230 --> 00:34:26,523
-You like it? What a relief.
-This is awesome.

773
00:34:26,606 --> 00:34:28,066
-Bravo.
-[Genta] Bravo!

774
00:34:28,858 --> 00:34:31,444
That was too close. I don't know why,
but I started tearing up.

775
00:34:31,528 --> 00:34:32,529
No, no, no.

776
00:34:32,612 --> 00:34:33,822
-Shall we dig in?
-Yeah?

777
00:34:33,905 --> 00:34:34,906
-Let's dig in.
-Bon Appétit!

778
00:34:34,990 --> 00:34:36,908
[band members] Thanks for the meal!
Digging in!

779
00:34:36,992 --> 00:34:38,868
-Hold on. Wait…
-[Shime] I'm over the moon.

780
00:34:39,369 --> 00:34:40,787
[laughing] Go, go!

781
00:34:40,870 --> 00:34:42,289
[Noel laughs]

782
00:34:42,372 --> 00:34:44,541
-You can't beat this.
-[Shizu] You're scarfing it down!

783
00:34:46,710 --> 00:34:47,877
[laughing]

784
00:34:47,961 --> 00:34:49,796
-[Shizu] You sure look happy.
-Well, time for me to chow down!

785
00:34:49,879 --> 00:34:51,089
-I'm digging in!
-Delicioso.

786
00:34:52,048 --> 00:34:53,091
[Shizu] Go for it.

787
00:34:56,052 --> 00:34:57,137
[laughing]

788
00:34:57,220 --> 00:34:58,221
-Yum!
-Time to give it a whirl.

789
00:34:58,305 --> 00:34:59,389
-[Shime] Yum!
-[laughs]

790
00:34:59,472 --> 00:35:00,807
-You're a genius taco chef!
-I'm glad.

791
00:35:00,890 --> 00:35:02,392
-Time to dig in.
-This is serious deliciousness.

792
00:35:02,475 --> 00:35:03,602
Yum!

793
00:35:03,685 --> 00:35:05,145
-[Shizu] Yum!
-What a decadent meal.

794
00:35:07,939 --> 00:35:08,940
[Machu, laughing] Yum!

795
00:35:09,608 --> 00:35:10,609
[in English] Check it out!

796
00:35:10,692 --> 00:35:12,319
[in Japanese] Mind if we share our spoils?

797
00:35:12,402 --> 00:35:14,362
-What?
-[Genta] It's a bit…

798
00:35:15,071 --> 00:35:17,699
[band members] What is it?

799
00:35:17,782 --> 00:35:19,451
Ta-da!

800
00:35:19,534 --> 00:35:20,744
[Chaka] Are those beer cans?

801
00:35:20,827 --> 00:35:22,245
[Genta] Ta-da!

802
00:35:22,329 --> 00:35:23,371
[Noel] What is it?

803
00:35:23,455 --> 00:35:24,873
[Genta, Machu] Ta-da!

804
00:35:25,582 --> 00:35:27,917
-[Genta] There. Ta-da!
-[Machu] Ta-da!

805
00:35:28,001 --> 00:35:32,547
We visited a brewery
and sampled a variety of beers.

806
00:35:32,631 --> 00:35:35,967
We then picked out drinks
that suit each member.

807
00:35:36,051 --> 00:35:39,137
-That's right, we picked out your drinks.
-Hold up! You drank?

808
00:35:39,220 --> 00:35:40,263
-I… did.
-[band members] What?

809
00:35:40,347 --> 00:35:41,765
-He had a sip!
-[band members cheer]

810
00:35:41,848 --> 00:35:43,516
[Machu] Shime had beer.

811
00:35:43,600 --> 00:35:44,934
-Good job!
-It was delicious.

812
00:35:45,018 --> 00:35:46,019
-[Shizu] Nice!
-[Umi] That's nuts.

813
00:35:46,102 --> 00:35:47,395
It wasn't a whole glass or anything.

814
00:35:47,479 --> 00:35:50,815
The brewery lets you try beer
right off the tap.

815
00:35:51,399 --> 00:35:53,526
I had a tiny sip of it.

816
00:35:54,027 --> 00:35:55,320
But it was out of this world.

817
00:35:55,403 --> 00:35:57,072
-They had something like that?
-All sorts of drinks.

818
00:35:57,155 --> 00:35:58,657
-[Machu] This one's for Noel.
-[Noel] Thanks.

819
00:35:59,157 --> 00:36:00,241
[Chaka] American brewery.

820
00:36:00,325 --> 00:36:01,326
-"Southwest coast."
-Yep.

821
00:36:01,409 --> 00:36:03,286
[Machu] Right. Here's Chaka's.

822
00:36:03,370 --> 00:36:04,496
-[in English] IPA.
-Thank you so much.

823
00:36:04,579 --> 00:36:06,414
[in Japanese] The one in front…
There it is. Here's Umi's.

824
00:36:06,498 --> 00:36:08,083
-Thanks.
-[Genta, in English] Oh, yes.

825
00:36:08,166 --> 00:36:09,751
[in Japanese] Then… Shizuya,

826
00:36:09,834 --> 00:36:11,795
we weren't sure which one you'd like,
so we got you two.

827
00:36:11,878 --> 00:36:13,963
-How thoughtful of you.
-That's considerate. You're a genius.

828
00:36:14,047 --> 00:36:15,924
-That's why there are eight cans.
-[Machu] Exactly.

829
00:36:16,007 --> 00:36:17,926
-I gotta have both then.
-[laughs]

830
00:36:18,009 --> 00:36:20,387
We've hardly had any drinks this trip.

831
00:36:20,470 --> 00:36:21,513
Really?

832
00:36:21,596 --> 00:36:22,597
[Shizu] Yum.

833
00:36:23,098 --> 00:36:24,766
-[Chaka] Delicious.
-[Umi] Good stuff.

834
00:36:24,849 --> 00:36:25,850
[Chaka] That's heavenly.

835
00:36:26,559 --> 00:36:27,769
This is delicious!

836
00:36:27,852 --> 00:36:30,772
-[Machu] It's good, right? Right? Right?
-[cheering]

837
00:36:30,855 --> 00:36:32,691
[Umi] My hands are filthy right now.
Sorry, guys.

838
00:36:32,774 --> 00:36:33,775
-You've got filthy hands!
-Yum.

839
00:36:33,858 --> 00:36:35,402
The drinks go well with the tacos.

840
00:36:35,485 --> 00:36:36,778
-Right?
-Yep, yep, yep, yep.

841
00:36:36,861 --> 00:36:38,988
-We went to a town called Durango.
-That's right. Durango.

842
00:36:39,072 --> 00:36:40,782
Team B isn't done yet!

843
00:36:40,865 --> 00:36:42,242
[Noel] What? You're kidding!

844
00:36:42,325 --> 00:36:43,326
-You're generous.
-Seriously?

845
00:36:43,410 --> 00:36:44,411
-Yep.
-Let's go!

846
00:36:44,494 --> 00:36:45,870
-Thank you, we appreciate it.
-Thank you.

847
00:36:45,954 --> 00:36:47,831
[Shime] We got each of you…

848
00:36:49,040 --> 00:36:50,291
-[Chaka] Is it more beer?
-What is it?

849
00:36:50,375 --> 00:36:51,376
-Beer?
-Doesn't look like it.

850
00:36:51,459 --> 00:36:52,585
-This is for you, Noel.
-Thank you!

851
00:36:52,669 --> 00:36:53,878
-Noel.
-[Chaka] Do we each get one?

852
00:36:53,962 --> 00:36:55,755
-[Genta] Oh, yeah!
-[Umi] I bet it's a beer starter.

853
00:36:55,839 --> 00:36:57,507
-Beer starter? How come?
-[Shime] Zuya-nii.

854
00:36:57,590 --> 00:36:58,591
[Shizu] Here. Thanks.

855
00:36:58,675 --> 00:37:00,093
-[Umi] Craft beer starter. Beer starter!
-[in English] Yeah.

856
00:37:00,176 --> 00:37:02,387
-[Shime, in Japanese] Umi.
-Thank you so much.

857
00:37:02,470 --> 00:37:07,142
We also picked out sachets
that suit each member.

858
00:37:07,225 --> 00:37:09,853
-That makes me smile.
-Chaka.

859
00:37:09,936 --> 00:37:12,856
-[Shime] Open it up, guys.
-[Umi] What's…

860
00:37:12,939 --> 00:37:14,232
-There it is.
-There it is!

861
00:37:14,315 --> 00:37:17,444
-[Noel] It's so pretty!
-[Umi] Wait a minute, Noel.

862
00:37:17,527 --> 00:37:19,946
What? What? What?

863
00:37:22,282 --> 00:37:24,951
-We're matching! [laughs]
-[band members] Matchy-matchy!

864
00:37:25,034 --> 00:37:26,453
[Machu] We're all matchy-matchy!

865
00:37:26,536 --> 00:37:27,996
[Noel] That's darling. Seriously?

866
00:37:28,079 --> 00:37:31,833
[Shime] We picked out stones
that suit each of you.

867
00:37:31,916 --> 00:37:33,418
We decided which ones to get together.

868
00:37:33,501 --> 00:37:35,670
The patterns differ,
but they're all the same type of stone.

869
00:37:35,754 --> 00:37:36,880
-That's right.
-That's what you did?

870
00:37:36,963 --> 00:37:38,423
Yeah. One important thing,

871
00:37:38,506 --> 00:37:41,801
you're supposed to wear it
against your skin. Tuck it in your shirt.

872
00:37:41,885 --> 00:37:42,886
[Noel] I see.

873
00:37:42,969 --> 00:37:46,306
[Genta] Wear it daily,
and it will ward off evil.

874
00:37:46,389 --> 00:37:47,432
That's wonderful.

875
00:37:47,515 --> 00:37:48,516
-I love it.
-It makes me smile.

876
00:37:48,600 --> 00:37:51,144
[Umi] Well, Team A
also has gifts for everyone…

877
00:37:51,227 --> 00:37:52,562
-Yep.
-[Genta] What?

878
00:37:52,645 --> 00:37:53,855
[Chaka] Yes. Shizu, you go first.

879
00:37:53,938 --> 00:37:55,231
Who is it for?

880
00:37:55,315 --> 00:37:56,816
It's for Shime-chan!

881
00:37:56,900 --> 00:37:58,526
[all exclaiming]

882
00:37:58,610 --> 00:37:59,778
-What, what?
-What is it?

883
00:37:59,861 --> 00:38:01,112
-[Chaka] Bubble Wrap.
-Bubble Wrap?

884
00:38:01,196 --> 00:38:03,740
-It will come in handy when you're moving.
-[Shizu] It's a gift for you.

885
00:38:04,866 --> 00:38:07,202
-It's cute!
-[Shizu] Yes. It's a stone bracelet!

886
00:38:07,285 --> 00:38:09,412
-I love it! It's very cute!
-How cute!

887
00:38:09,496 --> 00:38:12,916
-They told us that gemstones carry energy.
-Yes.

888
00:38:12,999 --> 00:38:18,254
Apparently, the stone draws power
from the surrounding elements.

889
00:38:18,838 --> 00:38:20,924
Next is a souvenir from me.

890
00:38:21,007 --> 00:38:22,592
-[Genta] Here comes.
-Chaka-chan!

891
00:38:22,675 --> 00:38:25,178
-My gift is for Genta.
-Thank you very much.

892
00:38:25,929 --> 00:38:28,181
Here you go. Here!

893
00:38:28,264 --> 00:38:29,974
[Machu] Wait…
We each get something different?

894
00:38:30,058 --> 00:38:31,518
We picked out different items
for each of you.

895
00:38:31,601 --> 00:38:33,061
-Hold on.
-What is it?

896
00:38:33,144 --> 00:38:35,021
-I'll open it when I get home.
-How come?

897
00:38:35,104 --> 00:38:37,273
-Open it now! That's the whole point.
-Come on, open it now.

898
00:38:37,357 --> 00:38:39,234
-[Chaka] Now's the time. Right now!
-You're an eager beaver.

899
00:38:39,317 --> 00:38:40,318
[Genta] Oh, wait!

900
00:38:40,401 --> 00:38:44,531
-This rocks! What the heck?
-[Chaka laughs] It's a dream catcher.

901
00:38:44,614 --> 00:38:46,991
-Whoa, this is so cute!
-[Shime] It's cute.

902
00:38:47,075 --> 00:38:50,245
They gave me a refresher on
what a dream catcher does.

903
00:38:50,328 --> 00:38:53,248
The threaded part is called a "spiderweb."

904
00:38:53,331 --> 00:38:57,669
-The middle?
-The web catches your nightmares.

905
00:38:58,253 --> 00:39:01,965
That's why it's best to
hang it in your bedroom.

906
00:39:02,048 --> 00:39:03,883
Then, do you see the rope
attached at the top?

907
00:39:03,967 --> 00:39:04,968
-This part?
-[Umi] Yep.

908
00:39:05,051 --> 00:39:07,846
[Chaka] The more nightmares it catches,
the more good luck it gives you.

909
00:39:07,929 --> 00:39:11,766
So hang it in your bedroom,
and it will get rid of bad energy.

910
00:39:11,850 --> 00:39:15,687
It will bring you good luck.
That's what they said.

911
00:39:15,770 --> 00:39:18,189
Thanks. I've been thinking about
getting one.

912
00:39:18,273 --> 00:39:19,274
-[Chaka] Actually?
-[Shizu] What?

913
00:39:19,357 --> 00:39:20,859
-[Chaka] Was it a perfect gift for you?
-It was.

914
00:39:20,942 --> 00:39:22,068
This one's for Kura.

915
00:39:22,151 --> 00:39:24,863
-What? I've no idea what it could be.
-Oh, yeah!

916
00:39:24,946 --> 00:39:26,865
-[Umi] You'll find out when you open it.
-Okay.

917
00:39:26,948 --> 00:39:29,534
-[Chaka] It's just the gift for Machu.
-Whoa, this is chunky.

918
00:39:29,617 --> 00:39:30,618
-[Machu] What?
-What is it?

919
00:39:32,704 --> 00:39:34,038
[laughs]

920
00:39:34,122 --> 00:39:35,665
[laughing]

921
00:39:35,748 --> 00:39:37,750
-[Genta] Oh, you…
-[Shizu] What is it? You like it or not?

922
00:39:37,834 --> 00:39:40,420
-[band members laugh]
-The heck is this?

923
00:39:40,503 --> 00:39:41,504
[Umi] This object? Well…

924
00:39:41,588 --> 00:39:43,840
[Chaka] The shopkeeper helped Kaito
pick it out.

925
00:39:44,924 --> 00:39:46,009
It's a pot.

926
00:39:46,092 --> 00:39:47,260
-[Machu] A pot?
-Yep. It's a pot.

927
00:39:47,343 --> 00:39:53,308
Yes, it's a clay pot. Let me explain.
It's a one of a kind.

928
00:39:53,391 --> 00:39:54,392
Okay.

929
00:39:54,475 --> 00:39:58,146
This artist is based in Monument Valley.

930
00:39:58,229 --> 00:40:01,858
They design each pot
and paint all of them by hand.

931
00:40:01,941 --> 00:40:03,276
-I see.
-That's incredible.

932
00:40:03,359 --> 00:40:05,236
-I feel so special.
-[Genta] It's cute.

933
00:40:05,320 --> 00:40:07,822
It's a handmade pot created
by a local artist, right?

934
00:40:07,906 --> 00:40:09,198
It's imbued with energy.

935
00:40:09,282 --> 00:40:11,242
Whoa, thanks a ton.

936
00:40:11,326 --> 00:40:13,620
-It suits you. It suits your hat too.
-It really does.

937
00:40:13,703 --> 00:40:14,704
What a perfect gift.

938
00:40:14,787 --> 00:40:16,831
-This will look great in my house.
-[Umi] Please put it up on display.

939
00:40:16,915 --> 00:40:18,541
-[Chaka] That's all the souvenirs from us.
-Yep.

940
00:40:18,625 --> 00:40:19,834
-What about mine?
-What?

941
00:40:19,918 --> 00:40:24,088
-We forgot. Just kidding, we didn't!
-Really?

942
00:40:24,172 --> 00:40:26,966
-The three of us picked this out for you.
-Thank you.

943
00:40:27,050 --> 00:40:29,052
-[Chaka] Here you go.
-[Umi] Then…

944
00:40:29,135 --> 00:40:30,136
[Shizu] This is for you.

945
00:40:30,219 --> 00:40:31,804
-Thank you. What is it?
-I'm dying to know!

946
00:40:31,888 --> 00:40:33,014
-[Shime] What is it?
-[Noel] Ready?

947
00:40:33,097 --> 00:40:34,515
-Go for it.
-[Noel] Ta-da.

948
00:40:34,599 --> 00:40:37,644
-Whoa! Kitty cats!
-[Machu] Oh, how cute.

949
00:40:37,727 --> 00:40:38,978
-[Noel] Aw, cute.
-[Shime] They're adorable.

950
00:40:39,062 --> 00:40:40,813
-Are those turquoises I see?
-[Machu] Look at their eyes.

951
00:40:40,897 --> 00:40:41,898
Turquoises are embedded in it.

952
00:40:41,981 --> 00:40:44,984
[Chaka] These are also
handmade Native American decors.

953
00:40:45,068 --> 00:40:49,197
How do I put it? It may not be a pot, but
it's still a type of handmade ceramics.

954
00:40:49,280 --> 00:40:50,865
-I love it. Thank you.
-[Shime] It's darling.

955
00:40:50,949 --> 00:40:54,202
-[Genta] It's very cute.
-Whoa, I love it. Thank you.

956
00:40:54,285 --> 00:40:55,453
-Thank you.
-Seriously, though. Thanks.

957
00:40:55,536 --> 00:40:56,537
Glad you like your gift.

958
00:40:56,621 --> 00:41:00,875
Well, I was hoping to hear
how the trip went for each of you.

959
00:41:01,501 --> 00:41:03,461
-You visited all sorts of places.
-We sure did.

960
00:41:03,544 --> 00:41:05,380
Perhaps you even visited places
I've never been.

961
00:41:05,463 --> 00:41:06,464
Right, right.

962
00:41:06,547 --> 00:41:09,300
So now, I want to hear about
the memorable moments from your trips.

963
00:41:09,384 --> 00:41:12,095
-I'd love to tell you mine. We really…
-Me too.

964
00:41:12,637 --> 00:41:19,143
We immersed ourselves in the traditions
and the culture everywhere we went.

965
00:41:19,686 --> 00:41:23,189
Taking it all in made me incredibly happy.

966
00:41:23,272 --> 00:41:24,440
I'm glad you feel that way.

967
00:41:24,524 --> 00:41:27,026
The fact that you planned it
made it even more special.

968
00:41:27,110 --> 00:41:30,363
That's great to hear. And now that we've
gathered together, we can talk about it.

969
00:41:30,446 --> 00:41:31,489
-Right?
-For sure.

970
00:41:31,572 --> 00:41:33,700
Like I said, I want to hear all about
the awesome moments.

971
00:41:33,783 --> 00:41:34,867
-That's true.
-[Genta] Great idea.

972
00:41:34,951 --> 00:41:37,578
I want to hear what you felt
and learned on this trip.

973
00:41:37,662 --> 00:41:39,372
-I see.
-[Machu] Of course you do.

974
00:41:39,455 --> 00:41:41,165
-Shizuya, wanna start us off?
-Should I?

975
00:41:41,249 --> 00:41:45,586
Well, let's see. Our trip was focused on
the United States' natural landscapes.

976
00:41:45,670 --> 00:41:46,879
-[Machu] Okay.
-It was all about nature.

977
00:41:46,963 --> 00:41:48,297
-Right. And…
-[Genta] Okay, okay.

978
00:41:48,381 --> 00:41:49,841
How do I say this? Well…

979
00:41:50,633 --> 00:41:54,512
I was hit by the majestic force of nature.
The raw power of the land, so to speak.

980
00:41:55,555 --> 00:41:57,140
We hiked up mountains too.

981
00:41:57,223 --> 00:41:58,224
Ah, of course.

982
00:41:58,307 --> 00:42:01,811
[Shizu] Yeah, we did that.
And then we met the Navajo.

983
00:42:01,894 --> 00:42:04,939
-[Chaka] That's right.
-[Shizu] Which is a Native Tribe.

984
00:42:05,023 --> 00:42:08,526
We had many wonderful encounters
with people and nature alike.

985
00:42:08,609 --> 00:42:10,028
[Chaka] We encountered
a completely foreign culture.

986
00:42:10,111 --> 00:42:11,821
Yes, it was a culture
we've never seen before.

987
00:42:11,904 --> 00:42:14,449
And we also rode horses.

988
00:42:14,532 --> 00:42:15,825
[Shime] Really?

989
00:42:15,908 --> 00:42:17,910
Horseback riding was a blast.

990
00:42:17,994 --> 00:42:18,995
[Genta] How nice.

991
00:42:19,078 --> 00:42:21,622
[Shizu] We had a great experience
with animals too.

992
00:42:21,706 --> 00:42:23,708
-We touched life itself.
-[Shizu] Exactly.

993
00:42:23,791 --> 00:42:25,084
-[Genta] I love that.
-[Machu] It sounds fantastic.

994
00:42:25,168 --> 00:42:26,502
[Noel] Umi, what about you?

995
00:42:26,586 --> 00:42:31,507
-[Umi] Oh, this trip was a blast.
-I was pretty worried about you.

996
00:42:31,591 --> 00:42:32,592
-[Shizu] How come?
-[Umi] Why?

997
00:42:32,675 --> 00:42:34,886
You aren't the type to venture out
into the wilderness.

998
00:42:34,969 --> 00:42:38,014
That's what we said about ourselves
at the start of the trip.

999
00:42:38,097 --> 00:42:41,809
[Noel] That's why I intentionally chose
the RV for Team A.

1000
00:42:41,893 --> 00:42:43,895
I based the whole trip around Kaito.

1001
00:42:43,978 --> 00:42:47,065
Every experience was chosen
with him in mind.

1002
00:42:47,607 --> 00:42:51,569
-We wondered why nature was our theme.
-[Shizu] Yeah, we talked about that.

1003
00:42:51,652 --> 00:42:53,071
In the beginning, we did. Hmm.

1004
00:42:53,154 --> 00:42:57,033
We thought it was
because the three of us are homebodies.

1005
00:42:57,116 --> 00:42:58,659
Yeah, we're homebodies.

1006
00:42:58,743 --> 00:43:02,121
But as we stepped into the great outdoors

1007
00:43:02,205 --> 00:43:06,542
and became one with nature…

1008
00:43:08,044 --> 00:43:11,214
and listened
to the Navajo people's stories…

1009
00:43:11,297 --> 00:43:15,468
we realized
there's so much we've yet to learn.

1010
00:43:15,968 --> 00:43:22,934
The Natives, who call themselves the Diné,
performed a special dance for us.

1011
00:43:23,017 --> 00:43:24,268
-[Machu] Whoa.
-[Shime] Yeah.

1012
00:43:24,352 --> 00:43:29,357
The performance is solely composed of
voice, percussion, and dance.

1013
00:43:29,440 --> 00:43:30,608
-[Genta] Huh.
-[Umi] Yeah.

1014
00:43:30,691 --> 00:43:35,071
The performance represents things
found in nature,

1015
00:43:35,154 --> 00:43:38,032
-such as horses or crows.
-[Genta] Whoa.

1016
00:43:38,116 --> 00:43:41,828
[Umi] As we watched the dance, we could
really tell the elements it represented.

1017
00:43:42,453 --> 00:43:45,748
Yes. At times, the dance resembled horses,
and at others, birds.

1018
00:43:46,582 --> 00:43:51,921
It was a reminder that you can enchant
an audience with something so simple.

1019
00:43:52,004 --> 00:43:56,717
I wanted to share
their powerful expression with everyone.

1020
00:43:57,510 --> 00:43:59,428
[Noel] Of course. I'm glad to hear that.

1021
00:43:59,512 --> 00:44:01,222
-Something about the mountain got to him.
-It called out to him.

1022
00:44:01,305 --> 00:44:03,975
[Shizu] Umi left us in the dust
and hiked up on his own!

1023
00:44:04,058 --> 00:44:05,476
-I didn't expect that.
-He zoomed past us.

1024
00:44:05,560 --> 00:44:06,561
[Shime] Did he really?

1025
00:44:06,644 --> 00:44:09,272
[Chaka] Noel, you mentioned
you were worried about Kaito.

1026
00:44:09,355 --> 00:44:10,648
But Kaito and nature, well…

1027
00:44:11,440 --> 00:44:15,528
It was almost like
he was conversing with nature.

1028
00:44:15,611 --> 00:44:16,612
Mmm, mmm.

1029
00:44:16,696 --> 00:44:21,534
Chaka, do you ever get on the move
seeking breathtaking landscapes?

1030
00:44:21,617 --> 00:44:25,121
[Chaka] Usually no. I don't go seeking
beautiful scenery on my own either.

1031
00:44:25,204 --> 00:44:26,205
[Machu] Right.

1032
00:44:26,289 --> 00:44:32,545
[Chaka] But the view was fantastic.
Really, it blew me away.

1033
00:44:32,628 --> 00:44:36,299
Words cannot describe
the magnificent views we encountered.

1034
00:44:36,382 --> 00:44:37,383
[Genta] Yeah.

1035
00:44:37,466 --> 00:44:40,178
[Chaka] It also can't describe
that we were awestruck.

1036
00:44:40,261 --> 00:44:42,346
[Shizu] It's true.
Words can't quite capture it.

1037
00:44:42,430 --> 00:44:45,433
Still, I'm grateful
we had this experience.

1038
00:44:46,642 --> 00:44:49,812
Also, it's been a while
since it was just the three of us.

1039
00:44:49,896 --> 00:44:51,856
[Genta] Yeah, we have our powerhouses,
Chaka, Umi, and Shizu.

1040
00:44:51,939 --> 00:44:54,400
You guys are powerhouses?

1041
00:44:54,483 --> 00:44:57,945
I thought about
how Travis Japan got started.

1042
00:44:58,029 --> 00:45:02,617
As you know, Shime and Noel were the older
members when the band was first formed.

1043
00:45:02,700 --> 00:45:05,953
The three of us, well… Travis Japan
started out with five members.

1044
00:45:06,037 --> 00:45:10,249
But the three of us
were always together at first.

1045
00:45:10,333 --> 00:45:14,337
Some moments on this trip
reminded me of those early days.

1046
00:45:14,420 --> 00:45:17,340
It also brought back memories of
Shizu and Umi from that time too.

1047
00:45:17,423 --> 00:45:23,054
The three of us have always worked hard.

1048
00:45:23,554 --> 00:45:30,228
And it was rewarding
to travel with them again.

1049
00:45:30,311 --> 00:45:34,482
We were stoked the entire trip. Like,
it's not that we've become besties, but…

1050
00:45:34,565 --> 00:45:36,984
-We tried to be considerate, yeah.
-The trip deepened our friendship.

1051
00:45:37,568 --> 00:45:41,739
But looking back and comparing it to now…

1052
00:45:42,240 --> 00:45:47,703
it was always the three of us
every step of the way.

1053
00:45:48,204 --> 00:45:50,748
And now, I hope the seven of us
can discover new sceneries together.

1054
00:45:50,831 --> 00:45:53,751
You know what? Hearing all this
makes me happy. It really does.

1055
00:45:53,834 --> 00:45:59,340
These three have adapted to nature
more than they realize.

1056
00:45:59,423 --> 00:46:00,841
-[chuckling] It's true.
-I'm glad.

1057
00:46:00,925 --> 00:46:03,302
-Thanks. I'm glad. Nice.
-[Umi] No, I had a lot of fun. Thanks.

1058
00:46:03,386 --> 00:46:05,554
-[Machu] How nice. Team A.
-[Shime] That was wonderful.

1059
00:46:06,097 --> 00:46:07,098
Machu, your turn.

1060
00:46:07,682 --> 00:46:09,850
-Actually, I want to hear from Genta.
-[Genta] Oh, sure. Okay.

1061
00:46:09,934 --> 00:46:12,270
Machu probably took away
the most from this trip.

1062
00:46:12,353 --> 00:46:13,854
-[Genta] It's true.
-That's what I think.

1063
00:46:13,938 --> 00:46:17,525
Well, I've always had a fascination

1064
00:46:17,608 --> 00:46:21,529
for Native American culture and designs.

1065
00:46:21,612 --> 00:46:26,200
On the trip, we saw many handmade crafts.

1066
00:46:26,284 --> 00:46:29,287
For instance,
we'd ask all about the artists

1067
00:46:29,370 --> 00:46:31,956
behind rugs, cushions,
and gem-studded jewelry.

1068
00:46:32,957 --> 00:46:35,209
There was so much
we gained from their stories.

1069
00:46:35,293 --> 00:46:37,878
Encountering culture and values

1070
00:46:37,962 --> 00:46:43,384
so different from Japan's
sent a shock right through me.

1071
00:46:43,467 --> 00:46:45,636
But like I said,
I love the Native American culture.

1072
00:46:45,720 --> 00:46:48,180
I thoroughly enjoyed immersing myself
in the local culture

1073
00:46:48,264 --> 00:46:51,642
and learning the history of the
United States through the locals' tales.

1074
00:46:52,226 --> 00:46:54,645
More than anything,
we've always worked together,

1075
00:46:54,729 --> 00:46:57,732
but I'd often find myself wondering
what the rest of you were doing.

1076
00:46:57,815 --> 00:46:59,984
We'd joke and say, "Do you think Zuya-nii…

1077
00:47:00,067 --> 00:47:01,235
-[laughing]
-…is being a Debbie Downer?"

1078
00:47:01,319 --> 00:47:02,320
We did say that, yeah.

1079
00:47:02,403 --> 00:47:04,947
Like, "Maybe Zuya-nii's at it,"

1080
00:47:05,031 --> 00:47:08,701
or like Noel said,
"Is Umi okay being out in the wild?"

1081
00:47:08,784 --> 00:47:14,540
Personally, I thought, "Chaka may
not find the scenery so striking."

1082
00:47:14,623 --> 00:47:17,960
I also thought Noel must be
going through a lot,

1083
00:47:18,044 --> 00:47:21,797
though I've no idea what's on his mind.

1084
00:47:21,881 --> 00:47:24,592
Especially because
you came up with this trip.

1085
00:47:25,301 --> 00:47:30,473
You probably had your reasons.
You may even have had expectations for us.

1086
00:47:30,556 --> 00:47:32,475
I'm sure things haven't been easy for you.

1087
00:47:32,558 --> 00:47:36,437
You must have a lot on your mind.

1088
00:47:36,520 --> 00:47:41,484
Even still, Travis Japan
never left my mind during the entire trip,

1089
00:47:41,567 --> 00:47:46,781
no matter where I was or what I was doing.

1090
00:47:46,864 --> 00:47:51,535
I'm grateful for TJ,
and I'm happy to be a part of it.

1091
00:47:52,036 --> 00:47:55,706
Now that our trip is over,
and we visited many different places,

1092
00:47:55,790 --> 00:47:58,417
I can proudly say I love TJ.

1093
00:47:58,501 --> 00:48:00,419
-[Chaka] Shime, what about you?
-[Shizu] Shime's next.

1094
00:48:00,503 --> 00:48:02,630
-[Chaka] I'd love to hear your thoughts.
-For me, well…

1095
00:48:02,713 --> 00:48:07,885
Well, it was so much fun.
I don't even know where to start.

1096
00:48:07,968 --> 00:48:10,221
-[Genta] Right.
-[Shime] We boarded a train.

1097
00:48:10,304 --> 00:48:11,722
You mean the Durango Silverton
Narrow Gauge Railroad.

1098
00:48:11,806 --> 00:48:14,809
-[Genta] Durango, yep.
-It was such a great experience.

1099
00:48:14,892 --> 00:48:16,894
The scenery we saw
from the train was just fantastic.

1100
00:48:16,977 --> 00:48:18,020
[Machu] It was great.

1101
00:48:18,104 --> 00:48:20,147
[Shime] It's like Big Thunder Mountain
in real life.

1102
00:48:20,231 --> 00:48:22,650
-[Machu] We're not even exaggerating.
-[Shime] It's not an attraction.

1103
00:48:22,733 --> 00:48:25,194
The city is like a theme park
brought to life.

1104
00:48:25,277 --> 00:48:28,072
The entire ride lasted about two hours.

1105
00:48:28,155 --> 00:48:30,074
Well, I can be a bit of a worrywart,

1106
00:48:30,157 --> 00:48:34,328
but during the train ride,
I kept thinking,

1107
00:48:34,412 --> 00:48:41,293
-"Why worry about every little thing?"
-[Machu] Mm-hmm.

1108
00:48:42,378 --> 00:48:47,842
And that was… Well…
it was a great experience for me.

1109
00:48:47,925 --> 00:48:49,510
-I see.
-[Shime] Yeah. That was…

1110
00:48:49,593 --> 00:48:53,722
-What did you think of Team B, Shime?
-The Team B trio.

1111
00:48:53,806 --> 00:48:56,016
We picked roles for the trip.

1112
00:48:56,100 --> 00:48:57,101
-[Shizu] What?
-[Noel] You did?

1113
00:48:57,184 --> 00:48:58,269
[Umi] Oh, really. Tell us about it.

1114
00:48:58,352 --> 00:49:01,480
What was it? Machu was
our designated driver and cameraman.

1115
00:49:01,564 --> 00:49:03,732
-He was your cameraman and the chauffeur.
-[Chaka] You had roles, I see.

1116
00:49:03,816 --> 00:49:04,817
-Machu did, yeah.
-Yeah.

1117
00:49:04,900 --> 00:49:08,946
Then, Gen-chan was in charge of
enjoying everything that came our way.

1118
00:49:09,029 --> 00:49:10,823
-He was the team cheerleader.
-The cheerleader, yeah.

1119
00:49:10,906 --> 00:49:12,241
[Genta] I tried to make everything fun.

1120
00:49:12,324 --> 00:49:13,534
-Easy.
-It's a perfect role for Genta.

1121
00:49:13,617 --> 00:49:15,202
-It was…
-An easy role to fill.

1122
00:49:15,286 --> 00:49:16,871
-[Shizu] The easiest one, huh?
-[Genta] Whatever.

1123
00:49:16,954 --> 00:49:19,874
-Then, Shime? What was your role?
-I was the group leader.

1124
00:49:19,957 --> 00:49:21,876
-The leader?
-[Machu] Yeah, Shime was our leader.

1125
00:49:21,959 --> 00:49:22,960
Shime, you're Team B's leader?

1126
00:49:23,043 --> 00:49:24,712
-He's the senior member out of us three.
-Yup.

1127
00:49:24,795 --> 00:49:25,796
[Genta] Shime is our leader.

1128
00:49:25,880 --> 00:49:28,757
-I'm usually never in a leadership role.
-[Chaka, Umi] Right.

1129
00:49:28,841 --> 00:49:31,177
-I had no idea what I was supposed to do.
-[Chaka] Yeah.

1130
00:49:31,260 --> 00:49:33,345
I thought, "Should I do
something special as the leader?

1131
00:49:33,429 --> 00:49:35,306
Should I try to be in charge?"

1132
00:49:35,389 --> 00:49:38,809
But in the end, I realized,
"No, I shouldn't worry about it too much."

1133
00:49:38,893 --> 00:49:40,019
[Machu chuckles]

1134
00:49:40,102 --> 00:49:41,103
The opposite of what you'd expect.

1135
00:49:41,187 --> 00:49:42,938
That's right,
the leader doesn't have to do anything.

1136
00:49:43,022 --> 00:49:45,024
Whatever, look at
how much you're shouldering!

1137
00:49:45,107 --> 00:49:47,151
[Shime] That was poorly worded.

1138
00:49:47,234 --> 00:49:49,612
It's not that leaders don't do anything.
It's about teamwork.

1139
00:49:49,695 --> 00:49:53,616
I had to let go of things
that were outside of my control.

1140
00:49:53,699 --> 00:49:54,700
Yeah.

1141
00:49:54,783 --> 00:49:57,703
But in those moments,
I had Machu and Genta to fall back on.

1142
00:49:57,786 --> 00:50:01,832
There were also times
when I had to step up and make decisions.

1143
00:50:01,916 --> 00:50:08,631
I learned the importance of interpersonal
relationships. There's a balance to it.

1144
00:50:08,714 --> 00:50:10,674
[Shizu] Right. The leader is the glue
that holds the group together.

1145
00:50:10,758 --> 00:50:12,676
-[Chaka] Noel, I bet you're over the moon.
-I really am.

1146
00:50:12,760 --> 00:50:13,969
I was so worried about you, Shime.

1147
00:50:14,053 --> 00:50:15,513
-[Shizu laughs]
-[Machu] Really, now?

1148
00:50:15,596 --> 00:50:18,474
I couldn't decide whether grouping
Machu and Genta together was a good idea.

1149
00:50:18,557 --> 00:50:21,810
Since Genta is already interested in
the Native American culture,

1150
00:50:21,894 --> 00:50:25,022
I thought Machu would be
a fun addition to the mix.

1151
00:50:25,105 --> 00:50:28,484
But then, I wasn't sure
how Shime would mesh with those two.

1152
00:50:28,567 --> 00:50:30,611
You know, Shime can be
a bit of an overthinker.

1153
00:50:30,694 --> 00:50:34,448
-Yeah.
-He tends to overanalyze everything.

1154
00:50:34,532 --> 00:50:36,325
I don't think it's a fault by any means,

1155
00:50:36,408 --> 00:50:41,372
but I was worried that Shime would be
self-conscious about his sensitive side.

1156
00:50:41,455 --> 00:50:42,456
[Shime] Right, right, right.

1157
00:50:42,540 --> 00:50:46,210
I hoped you'd open your mind…

1158
00:50:46,293 --> 00:50:49,004
-[Shime] Yeah. Mm-hmm.
-…even by a bit, on this trip.

1159
00:50:49,088 --> 00:50:50,464
What you said makes me really happy.

1160
00:50:50,548 --> 00:50:51,882
I learned to be more open to uncertainty.

1161
00:50:51,966 --> 00:50:52,967
-[Noel] I'm glad.
-Yep.

1162
00:50:53,050 --> 00:50:54,927
Let me tell you, he's a good leader.

1163
00:50:55,511 --> 00:50:57,346
-[band members] Yeah?
-He's a comforting presence.

1164
00:50:57,429 --> 00:50:58,556
[Genta] Comforting… He's a peacekeeper.

1165
00:50:59,640 --> 00:51:01,767
-He was a great leader.
-[Shime] You mean it?

1166
00:51:01,850 --> 00:51:03,727
[band members laugh]

1167
00:51:03,811 --> 00:51:05,062
-He downed his glass!
-He chugged it!

1168
00:51:05,145 --> 00:51:06,730
-[Machu] That was tequila!
-TJ's leader downed his drink!

1169
00:51:06,814 --> 00:51:11,026
Well, honestly, Chaka wasn't much of
a leader for us, but he did all right.

1170
00:51:11,110 --> 00:51:12,152
[band members laugh]

1171
00:51:12,236 --> 00:51:15,864
-Is that supposed to make me feel better?
-He's so bad at comforting people, huh?

1172
00:51:15,948 --> 00:51:17,533
-I'm in pure bliss.
-Come on, everyone…

1173
00:51:17,616 --> 00:51:19,201
[Chaka] We want to hear
your experience now.

1174
00:51:19,285 --> 00:51:21,287
-[Chaka] You're the poet among us.
-Very true.

1175
00:51:21,370 --> 00:51:23,080
[Chaka] I'd love to hear your thoughts.

1176
00:51:23,163 --> 00:51:29,461
Well… It was so much fun,
and I learned a bunch.

1177
00:51:30,045 --> 00:51:32,923
Genta and Shime touched on it,

1178
00:51:33,007 --> 00:51:35,843
but there's a lot you never learn

1179
00:51:35,926 --> 00:51:39,680
unless you go out
and experience things firsthand.

1180
00:51:39,763 --> 00:51:41,056
Hmm.

1181
00:51:41,140 --> 00:51:44,184
Then… how do I put it?

1182
00:51:45,686 --> 00:51:46,687
Let's see…

1183
00:51:49,315 --> 00:51:51,817
-And… Nope, I'm not gonna cry. Nope.
-[Umi] You're gonna cry.

1184
00:51:53,819 --> 00:51:54,820
It's like…

1185
00:51:54,903 --> 00:51:57,615
[Chaka] It's okay to cry.
We're all sharing fond memories.

1186
00:51:57,698 --> 00:51:59,033
What do I even say…

1187
00:51:59,116 --> 00:52:01,910
Simply put, on day one,

1188
00:52:01,994 --> 00:52:08,959
we said we wanted to find out
why Noel chose the three of us as Team B

1189
00:52:09,043 --> 00:52:14,214
by the end of the trip.

1190
00:52:14,298 --> 00:52:16,967
To be completely honest, on day one,
we couldn't tell you.

1191
00:52:17,051 --> 00:52:18,052
[Shime] Right.

1192
00:52:18,135 --> 00:52:23,015
But it'd be nice if we can get to
the bottom of why you planned this trip.

1193
00:52:23,098 --> 00:52:26,644
But to be honest,
I still don't have an answer for you.

1194
00:52:26,727 --> 00:52:27,811
Well, that's fine.

1195
00:52:27,895 --> 00:52:31,106
I can't tell you what Noel wanted,
but on this trip,

1196
00:52:31,190 --> 00:52:33,859
we had so many wonderful encounters.

1197
00:52:33,942 --> 00:52:39,823
You can't learn about a different culture
unless you go and experience it firsthand.

1198
00:52:39,907 --> 00:52:43,535
That's my takeaway from this trip.

1199
00:52:43,619 --> 00:52:45,663
The only way to learn
is through encounters.

1200
00:52:45,746 --> 00:52:48,624
As important as it is
to learn about different cultures,

1201
00:52:48,707 --> 00:52:50,084
we were also deeply touched by

1202
00:52:50,167 --> 00:52:52,336
the kindness of all the locals
we met along the way.

1203
00:52:52,419 --> 00:52:53,420
Right.

1204
00:52:54,380 --> 00:53:00,094
[Machu] Anyhow, it was
a heartwarming trip. That's for sure.

1205
00:53:01,011 --> 00:53:04,056
I don't even know
what I was getting at anymore.

1206
00:53:04,139 --> 00:53:05,516
-What's wrong with that?
-[Noel] Machu, you…

1207
00:53:05,599 --> 00:53:09,436
-You had many wonderful experiences.
-I thought that's where you'd land, Machu.

1208
00:53:09,520 --> 00:53:10,521
[band members] Right.

1209
00:53:10,604 --> 00:53:14,983
I know we all have
our personal ambitions and goals,

1210
00:53:15,067 --> 00:53:18,570
but I also know
just how tender-hearted you are, Machu.

1211
00:53:18,654 --> 00:53:20,989
I knew it'd take you some time
to find an answer

1212
00:53:21,073 --> 00:53:23,951
while you experience
so many new things at once.

1213
00:53:24,034 --> 00:53:25,869
You'll take your time
processing everything,

1214
00:53:25,953 --> 00:53:27,663
but eventually, you'll find your answer.

1215
00:53:27,746 --> 00:53:29,331
Then, you'll push forward
and pave your own path.

1216
00:53:29,415 --> 00:53:33,085
I know that's who you are, Machu.

1217
00:53:33,627 --> 00:53:34,712
[♪ gentle music playing]

1218
00:53:34,795 --> 00:53:37,756
I figured you'd be the last one
to find your answer.

1219
00:53:37,840 --> 00:53:40,467
So you don't need to
give us an answer now.

1220
00:53:40,551 --> 00:53:42,970
You don't have to know…

1221
00:53:43,053 --> 00:53:48,434
Machu, you don't have to know
what this trip meant for you right away.

1222
00:53:48,517 --> 00:53:50,769
Actually, that's very like you.

1223
00:53:50,853 --> 00:53:51,979
[Genta, Shime] Right, right.

1224
00:53:52,062 --> 00:53:53,605
I hope some day,

1225
00:53:53,689 --> 00:53:56,650
when you look back on this trip,
you can say it was a good experience.

1226
00:53:56,734 --> 00:53:58,360
It may have been Team B's experience,

1227
00:53:58,444 --> 00:54:00,487
but at the same time,
this is your experience, Machu.

1228
00:54:01,029 --> 00:54:05,451
Hopefully, the answer you reach
will include all seven of us somehow.

1229
00:54:05,534 --> 00:54:09,747
[Machu, voice breaking] But…
we parted ways and learned a ton.

1230
00:54:09,830 --> 00:54:13,834
It was such a lighthearted, fun trip.

1231
00:54:13,917 --> 00:54:17,171
We've been together since day…
the entire time, we…

1232
00:54:17,254 --> 00:54:19,465
-[Genta imitates Machu] Day…
-[band members laugh]

1233
00:54:19,548 --> 00:54:24,928
It was so fun, and we talked a ton,
and we learned a bunch of fun things.

1234
00:54:25,012 --> 00:54:28,891
We guessed what you wanted us
to learn on this trip.

1235
00:54:28,974 --> 00:54:33,604
Well, we saw so many
breathtaking landscapes.

1236
00:54:33,687 --> 00:54:36,565
But there's one thing I can say for sure.

1237
00:54:36,648 --> 00:54:39,276
I felt so at ease
when I finally saw everyone again.

1238
00:54:39,359 --> 00:54:40,694
-Oh, you…
-[Chaka] Stop talking.

1239
00:54:40,778 --> 00:54:42,654
[Genta] Stop it. Don't talk anymore.

1240
00:54:42,738 --> 00:54:45,449
[Umi] But because we went on this trip,

1241
00:54:45,532 --> 00:54:49,453
we can talk so openly
about how we feel right now.

1242
00:54:49,536 --> 00:54:52,748
-[Genta, chuckling] Umi's crying!
-[band members laugh]

1243
00:54:52,831 --> 00:54:56,335
[Genta] Umi's crying in front of people…

1244
00:54:56,877 --> 00:54:58,003
[Chaka] It's a bit…

1245
00:54:58,086 --> 00:54:59,338
[Genta] Chaka's tearing up too.

1246
00:54:59,421 --> 00:55:05,177
[Chaka] Oh, man, how do I say this,
I'm touched by everything you just said.

1247
00:55:06,345 --> 00:55:12,518
Distance made my heart grow fonder for TJ.

1248
00:55:13,310 --> 00:55:16,772
We had all these wonderful experiences
with our teams.

1249
00:55:16,855 --> 00:55:20,859
But Noel, he was on his own this time.

1250
00:55:20,943 --> 00:55:22,819
We don't know everything he's done for us.

1251
00:55:22,903 --> 00:55:28,534
All we can do is keep trying to guess
why he sent us on this trip.

1252
00:55:28,617 --> 00:55:35,582
But Noel's, well…
How Noel feels is the most…

1253
00:55:35,666 --> 00:55:36,667
Right?

1254
00:55:36,750 --> 00:55:39,711
[Chaka] There must be a lot
going through your head right now.

1255
00:55:39,795 --> 00:55:41,797
After all, we were apart for a while.

1256
00:55:42,756 --> 00:55:49,555
Could you tell us your thoughts?

1257
00:55:50,055 --> 00:55:52,891
-I just wonder, what was the point?
-[Umi] Yeah, we'd like to hear from you.

1258
00:55:52,975 --> 00:55:55,018
We're not asking you
to give us all the answers.

1259
00:55:55,102 --> 00:55:57,771
I'll be frank.
I don't have an answer for you.

1260
00:55:57,854 --> 00:56:03,402
Each of you brings
a unique personality to Travis Japan.

1261
00:56:03,485 --> 00:56:07,281
Everything we've accomplished is
because of what you bring to the table.

1262
00:56:07,364 --> 00:56:10,117
You're the parts
that make Travis Japan whole.

1263
00:56:10,200 --> 00:56:13,078
So, there isn't a single answer
I could give you.

1264
00:56:13,662 --> 00:56:15,956
I don't know…
I don't quite know how to say this.

1265
00:56:17,249 --> 00:56:23,547
Anyway, I also had time to reflect
while we were apart.

1266
00:56:24,256 --> 00:56:27,676
I thought, I want Travis Japan
to be the seven of us.

1267
00:56:27,759 --> 00:56:34,266
And the times we spend together are
the most precious moments of my life.

1268
00:56:35,100 --> 00:56:37,269
That's why I want
to keep doing this with you.

1269
00:56:37,352 --> 00:56:40,981
The time we spend looking after
one another is important too,

1270
00:56:41,064 --> 00:56:47,904
but when we grouped up,
it gave everyone some time to reflect.

1271
00:56:47,988 --> 00:56:53,577
I thought we can become
more united as a band

1272
00:56:53,660 --> 00:56:57,122
if each of us brings back the answers
we found to Travis Japan.

1273
00:56:58,081 --> 00:57:00,500
When you shared your experiences just now,

1274
00:57:00,584 --> 00:57:06,006
it showed me
that you didn't squander the vacation.

1275
00:57:06,089 --> 00:57:10,177
Each of you tried to
tie meanings to the trip,

1276
00:57:10,260 --> 00:57:13,764
and reflected on how you can better
contribute to Travis Japan.

1277
00:57:14,931 --> 00:57:20,437
I'm so happy that this trip
wasn't lost on any of you.

1278
00:57:20,520 --> 00:57:24,483
And maybe, that's the answer
I was hoping to find for Travis Japan.

1279
00:57:24,566 --> 00:57:28,445
-I'm overcome with joy.
-[Chaka] Mmm.

1280
00:57:28,528 --> 00:57:34,201
I'm glad I had the chance to think about
what I can do for everyone,

1281
00:57:34,284 --> 00:57:40,457
and hopefully I showed you
what I want to bring to Travis Japan.

1282
00:57:41,667 --> 00:57:44,711
I sincerely wish for the seven of us

1283
00:57:44,795 --> 00:57:49,007
to continue setting forth on adventures
as Travis Japan. [sniffles]

1284
00:57:49,591 --> 00:57:53,387
Man, was it the time of our lives,
or what?

1285
00:57:53,470 --> 00:57:57,015
-Well… we're not out of time yet, are we?
-That's right.

1286
00:57:57,099 --> 00:57:58,350
-Our journey will go on.
-Yeah.

1287
00:57:58,433 --> 00:58:00,102
Exactly. Our trip isn't over yet.

1288
00:58:00,185 --> 00:58:01,853
[Genta] Our trip isn't over?
We're not done just yet.

1289
00:58:01,937 --> 00:58:04,147
-We're finally together.
-We're all together after all this time.

1290
00:58:04,231 --> 00:58:06,274
-That's right, finally, we've…
-[Chaka] Oh, but…

1291
00:58:06,358 --> 00:58:09,152
-You've only been on the road for a week.
-[band members] That's right.

1292
00:58:09,236 --> 00:58:12,406
[Genta] But I really missed you guys
after just a week.

1293
00:58:12,489 --> 00:58:15,867
Let's do the cheer.
Then, we'll plan tomorrow's trip.

1294
00:58:15,951 --> 00:58:20,706
That's right,
we'll create a plan together.

1295
00:58:20,789 --> 00:58:21,998
The trip isn't over yet.

1296
00:58:22,082 --> 00:58:23,750
-We've got some time left!
-This is a story you two started.

1297
00:58:23,834 --> 00:58:24,668
Machu.

1298
00:58:24,751 --> 00:58:26,920
It's thanks to you
that we have our special cheer.

1299
00:58:27,003 --> 00:58:29,881
Noel, why don't you lead us?
To our next adventure.

1300
00:58:29,965 --> 00:58:33,009
Well, Travis Japan, um…

1301
00:58:33,802 --> 00:58:37,848
We've got no time… [sniffles]
…to be a-wasting.

1302
00:58:37,931 --> 00:58:43,937
I mean it when I say we'll be together
until we're as wrinkled as prunes.

1303
00:58:44,938 --> 00:58:47,607
We'll bring back what we learned
to Travis Japan.

1304
00:58:48,608 --> 00:58:54,573
We'll embark on many, many more
spectacular journeys together. Agreed?

1305
00:58:54,656 --> 00:58:56,241
[all] Agreed!

1306
00:58:57,159 --> 00:59:00,245
Let's go, TJ! Let's go!

1307
00:59:00,328 --> 00:59:02,998
[all] Thank you! [chuckle]

1308
01:00:13,527 --> 01:00:15,529
Translated by Megumi Hunter
